<div id="alg2.6.18" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.6.18.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.6.18.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">16</span></span>
                <math id="alg2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i,k,t}\leftarrow x_{i,k,t}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i,k,t}\leftarrow x_{i,k,t}+1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.6.18.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.19" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.6.19.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">17</span></span>
                <span id="alg2.6.19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.20" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.6.20.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.6.20.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.20.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">18</span></span>
                <span id="alg2.6.20.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">return</span><span id="alg2.6.20.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="alg2.6.20.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Failed</span><span id="alg2.6.20.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.21" class="ltx_listingline">
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">19</span></span>
                <span id="alg2.6.21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">return</span><span id="alg2.6.21.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><math id="alg2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.6.21.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The preemption scheduling (Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="In Preemptive Scheduling ‣ 3.4.2. Preemption-aware Scheduling Policy ‣ 3.4. Preemptive Task Scheduler (PTS) ‣ 3. Design of GFS ‣ GFS: A Preemption-aware Scheduling Framework for GPU Clusters with Predictive Spot Instance Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) employs a waste-aware heuristic. It obtains the set of all spot tasks <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> running on all candidate nodes in <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> (lines 5-7). For each spot task <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}\in\mathcal{T}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}\in\mathcal{T}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we calculate the resource waste due to preemption, resulting in unsaved states:</p>
<table id="S3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta_{\tau_{s}}=g_{\tau_{j}}\cdot(t-t^{check}_{\tau_{s}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta_{\tau_{s}}=g_{\tau_{j}}\cdot(t-t^{check}_{\tau_{s}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\tau_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\tau_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the requested GPUs of <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t-t^{check}_{\tau_{s}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t-t^{check}_{\tau_{s}})</annotation></semantics></math> represents the elapsed time since last checkpoint. By sorting candidates in descending order of wastes (line 8), the algorithm prioritizes preserving high-value tasks that are likely nearing the completion of guaranteed hours (checkpoints). Moreover, the linear scan (lines 9–13) ensures <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(|\mathcal{T}_{k}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(|\mathcal{T}_{k}|)</annotation></semantics></math> complexity while achieving near-optimal solutions.
The final GPU selection (lines 14-18) aims to ensure that the spot tasks in <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> running on node <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with the lowest preemption cost are chosen. The preemption cost for node <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is calculate by:</p>
<table id="S3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cost(n_{k})=\underbrace{\frac{F+|\mathcal{T}_{k}|}{G+F+|\mathcal{T}_{k}|}-\frac{F}{G+F}}_{\text{Eviction rate impact}}+\beta\cdot\underbrace{\frac{\sum_{\tau_{s}\in\mathcal{T}_{k}}\vartheta_{\tau_{s}}}{\sum_{k=1}^{M}S_{k}\cdot T}}_{\text{Usage impact}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Eviction rate impact</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Usage impact</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cost(n_{k})=\underbrace{\frac{F+|\mathcal{T}_{k}|}{G+F+|\mathcal{T}_{k}|}-\frac{F}{G+F}}_{\text{Eviction rate impact}}+\beta\cdot\underbrace{\frac{\sum_{\tau_{s}\in\mathcal{T}_{k}}\vartheta_{\tau_{s}}}{\sum_{k=1}^{M}S_{k}\cdot T}}_{\text{Usage impact}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> represent the number of historical successful and evicted spot tasks, respectively in the cluster, and <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{k}\cdot T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{k}\cdot T</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the total execution time of GPUs in node <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the term <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{F}{G+F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{F}{G+F}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E18" title="In Preemptive Scheduling ‣ 3.4.2. Preemption-aware Scheduling Policy ‣ 3.4. Preemptive Task Scheduler (PTS) ‣ 3. Design of GFS ‣ GFS: A Preemption-aware Scheduling Framework for GPU Clusters with Predictive Spot Instance Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) is a constant for total nodes, the simplified cost metric becomes:</p>
<table id="S3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cost(n_{k})=\frac{F+|\mathcal{T}_{k}|}{G+F+|\mathcal{T}_{k}|}+\ \beta\cdot\frac{\sum_{\tau_{s}\in\mathcal{T}_{k}}\vartheta_{\tau_{s}}}{\sum_{k=1}^{M}S_{k}\cdot T}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cost(n_{k})=\frac{F+|\mathcal{T}_{k}|}{G+F+|\mathcal{T}_{k}|}+\ \beta\cdot\frac{\sum_{\tau_{s}\in\mathcal{T}_{k}}\vartheta_{\tau_{s}}}{\sum_{k=1}^{M}S_{k}\cdot T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">PTS selects nodes with the minimal <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cost(n_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cost(n_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, balancing eviction rates and resource usage through <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. This design ensures that the system remains aligned with the overarching optimization objective.
Finally, the entire process of PTS is outlined in Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="In Preemptive Scheduling ‣ 3.4.2. Preemption-aware Scheduling Policy ‣ 3.4. Preemptive Task Scheduler (PTS) ‣ 3. Design of GFS ‣ GFS: A Preemption-aware Scheduling Framework for GPU Clusters with Predictive Spot Instance Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. The time complexity of Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.4.2. Preemption-aware Scheduling Policy ‣ 3.4. Preemptive Task Scheduler (PTS) ‣ 3. Design of GFS ‣ GFS: A Preemption-aware Scheduling Framework for GPU Clusters with Predictive Spot Instance Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mid w_{i}\mid\mid\mathcal{G}\mid)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">∣</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mid w_{i}\mid\mid\mathcal{G}\mid)</annotation></semantics></math>, and Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="In Preemptive Scheduling ‣ 3.4.2. Preemption-aware Scheduling Policy ‣ 3.4. Preemptive Task Scheduler (PTS) ‣ 3. Design of GFS ‣ GFS: A Preemption-aware Scheduling Framework for GPU Clusters with Predictive Spot Instance Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mid w_{i}\mid\mid\mathcal{G}\mid\mid\mathcal{T}_{k}\mid)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.0835em">∣</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∣</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em">∣</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mid w_{i}\mid\mid\mathcal{G}\mid\mid\mathcal{T}_{k}\mid)</annotation></semantics></math>, so PTS’s time complexity is <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mid w_{i}\mid\mid\mathcal{G}\mid\mid\mathcal{T}_{k}\mid)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.0835em">∣</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∣</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em">∣</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mid w_{i}\mid\mid\mathcal{G}\mid\mid\mathcal{T}_{k}\mid)</annotation></semantics></math>. The average time to schedule a task is &lt; 1 second in our implementation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span>Preemptive Task Scheduler (PTS)</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
